{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevLL2wvRZ4c7CEXNyLK9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n```\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a cancellation capability to orders where cancelling an active order sets its status to CANCELLED, cancels all CREATED shipments, and enforces business rules around CONFIRMED shipments and duplicate cancellations.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n\n- `Order.kt:11-16` — Order entity lacks status field\n- `OrderController.kt:21-34` — POST /orders creates but doesn't initialize status\n- `OrderController.kt:36-42` — GET /orders/{orderId} returns Order\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` — Shipment has status field already (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt` — No method to find shipments by orderId\n- `ShipmentController.kt:26-44` — POST /shipments creates shipments without checking order status\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:11-30` — Exception hierarchy exists with ResourceNotFoundException and ConflictException\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum needs new code for cancelled order shipment rejection\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n\n- Controllers throw `ApiException` subclasses; `GlobalExceptionHandler` converts them to JSON\n- Error responses use `ApiError` with code, message, and optional fields\n- Tests use MockMvc with `@SpringBootTest` and `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`\n- Repositories are in-memory with clear() for test setup\n- `CreateOrder/ShipmentRequest` DTOs separate from entities\n- HTTP status codes: 201 for created, 404 for not found, 409 for conflict\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. `Order.kt` — Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class and define OrderStatus enum\n2. `OrderController.kt` — Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint and modify POST /orders to set initial status\n3. `OrderRepository.kt` — Add methods to find shipments by orderId (actually needs ShipmentRepository)\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — Add method to find all shipments by orderId\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add check in POST /shipments to reject if order is CANCELLED\n6. `ApiError.kt` — Add error code for cancelled order shipment rejection\n7. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — Add tests for cancel endpoint\n8. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add test for shipment rejection on cancelled order\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- Breaking existing tests by adding required status field to Order\n- Order creation needs to initialize status to ACTIVE\n- Shipment cancellation must be atomic with order cancellation (all-or-nothing)\n- Need to handle concurrent access to orders and shipments (already using ConcurrentHashMap)\n- Shipment creation must check order exists before checking its status (avoid confusing 404 vs 409)\n\n**Open questions:**\n\nNone identified. The ticket clearly defines all cases: ACTIVE→CANCELLED transition, already CANCELLED idempotency, CONFIRMED rejection, non-existent order 404, and shipment creation on cancelled order 409.\n\n---\n\nNow let me proceed to the DESIGN phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order. Add `OrderStatus` enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED. OrderStatus will be initialized to ACTIVE on order creation by the controller.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — \n   - Modify POST /orders to set `status = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` when creating\n   - Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that:\n     - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n     - If order is ACTIVE: change to CANCELLED, get all shipments for this order, cancel all CREATED ones, save order, return cancelled order\n     - If order is CANCELLED: return order unchanged (idempotent, no change)\n     - If any shipment is CONFIRMED: return 409 ConflictException without changing anything\n   - The cancel logic must check all shipments first before making any changes\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to fetch all shipments for an order\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — \n   - Inject OrderRepository to check order status\n   - In POST /shipments create method, after checking for duplicate shipment:\n     - Find the order; if it doesn't exist, current behavior (no explicit order check, likely won't create)\n     - If order exists and is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with new error code\n     - Continue with normal creation if order is ACTIVE\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code for when trying to create a shipment for a cancelled order\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add tests for:\n   - Cancel an ACTIVE order returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n   - Cancel an order twice succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancel an order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n   - Cancel a non-existent order returns 404\n   - Cancelling cancels all CREATED shipments\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test for:\n   - Attempting to create shipment on CANCELLED order returns 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n\nI considered making ShipmentRepository a dependency of OrderController to cancel shipments directly, but that would reverse the normal dependency direction. Instead, OrderController gets all shipments via ShipmentRepository (which will be injected) and updates them directly.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order:**\n   - GET order from repo\n   - GET all shipments for that order\n   - CHECK: no shipment is CONFIRMED → if any is, throw 409, exit\n   - UPDATE: set order.status = CANCELLED\n   - UPDATE: for each CREATED shipment, set status = CANCELLED\n   - SAVE order\n   - SAVE all shipments\n   - RETURN order (status: CANCELLED, HTTP 200)\n\n2. **Cancel already CANCELLED order:**\n   - GET order from repo\n   - RETURN order unchanged (status: CANCELLED, HTTP 200)\n\n3. **Cancel non-existent order:**\n   - GET order from repo → null\n   - THROW ResourceNotFoundException (HTTP 404)\n\n4. **Create shipment on CANCELLED order:**\n   - GET order from repo\n   - IF order.status == CANCELLED: THROW ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED (HTTP 409)\n   - Else: continue with normal creation\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n*OrderControllerTest:*\n- `cancel_active_order_succeeds` — Create order, cancel it, verify status is CANCELLED\n- `cancel_active_order_cancels_created_shipments` — Create order, create CREATED shipments, cancel order, verify shipments are CANCELLED\n- `cancel_order_twice_succeeds` — Cancel order, cancel again, verify second returns success\n- `cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment_fails` — Create order, create shipment, manually set to CONFIRMED, cancel, verify 409 and order still ACTIVE\n- `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404` — Cancel non-existent order, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n\n*ShipmentControllerTest:*\n- `create_shipment_on_cancelled_order_fails` — Create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n---\n\nNow I'll proceed with IMPLEMENTATION.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me start by modifying the Order entity to add status:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1379,"cache_read_input_tokens":17925,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1379},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7bfb387-b954-4db1-af3d-d1aff8fad5a0","uuid":"06a77136-f902-46b6-b07f-3096c31c0ce4","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:46:18.396Z","request_id":"req_011CevLL2GVjWqbmN7bHdHoj"}
